Lite Switcher - third party data

The language packs in LiteraryLanguages/ contain frequency data derived from:

- FrequencyWords by Hermit Dave (https://github.com/hermitdave/FrequencyWords),
  content licensed under CC BY-SA 4.0, built from OpenSubtitles (https://www.opensubtitles.org,
  OPUS). Used for the English, Russian and Ukrainian packs (the 2018 lists).

The derived files (words.fst, ngram3.bin) are provided under the same licence, see LICENSE-DATA.
The program code is licensed under the MIT licence, see LICENSE.

The programming pack of 1C (ProgrammingLanguages/1c) is not distributed with the source: its dictionary
is built from the seed list in the repository (the syntax of the language, written for this project)
and, on the machine of the builder, from the names of the platform API and from private code. The
built dictionary is never committed. The seed list is under the MIT licence like the code.
The local lexicon (ProgrammingLanguages/*/local) is made from the user's own code and is never
committed or published.

The sources and licences of every data source are described in docs/data-sources.md.
